@startuml router-controller-sequence
title MAVLink Router Node: Startup, Standby Mode & ROS 2 Apply Sequence

participant "Docker / Systemd" as Init
participant "MavlinkRouter\n(Process Manager)" as Router
participant "MavlinkRouterNode\n(ROS 2 Node)" as Node
participant "Linux Process\n(mavlink-routerd)" as RouterD
participant "Serial Devices\n(UART)" as UART
participant "QGC / Operator\n(UDP :14550)" as QGC
participant "ConfigAgent\n(UDP :14600)" as Agent

== Startup & Standby Check ==
Init -> Router : start() before rclcpp::init()
Router -> Router : read /run/drone/links.json (or config/links.json)
Router -> Router : generate_config_content()
Router -> RouterD : fork() & execvp("mavlink-routerd", "-c", conf)
Init -> Node : rclcpp::init() & spin()

== Steady-State Telemetry Routing ==
UART -> RouterD : MAVLink frames
RouterD -> QGC : UDP :14550 (GCS Telemetry)
RouterD -> Agent : UDP :14600 (Config Agent)
Node -> Node : 1 Hz timer -> publish /cc/serial_link_status

== Dynamic Configuration Apply via ROS 2 ==
Agent -> Node : Service /cc/router/apply_links
Node -> Router : apply_links(new_links)
Router -> Router : lock config_mutex_, generate_config_file()
Router -> RouterD : kill(SIGTERM) & waitpid(), then spawn new routerd
Node -> Agent : response success=true

== Hotplug Watchdog (every 5 s) ==
Router -> Router : check child_alive & port availability
alt child died OR serial port changed
  Router -> Router : restart child process
end

@enduml
